DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTSTAMP:20260910T165449Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53020733796497-53020733956347@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Moments in the History of East Asian Printing brings together 
 rare books\, facsimiles\, woodblocks\, broadsheets\, illustrated books\, t
 ypewriter materials\, and other objects from the East Asia Library’s col
 lections. The exhibit explores selected episodes in the history of printin
 g across China\, Korea\, and Japan\, from Buddhist woodblock printing and 
 movable type to lithography\, popular publishing\, travel prints\, visual 
 encyclopedias\, and the Chinese typewriter. Rather than offering a complet
 e chronol\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-10 09:54 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford University Libraries] Text Machines: Scarlet Thread of t
 he Digital Order (1883-2026)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTSTAMP:20260910T165449Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53251159287291-53251159382626@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Stanford Libraries now holds an 1883 edition of a rare book\,
  Les laboureurs: poème tiré de Jocelyn\, whose pages (text and ornamen
 ts) were entirely woven on a Jacquard loom by the firm of silk merchant Jo
 seph-Alphonse Henry. This exhibition explores the cultural contexts and ma
 terial conditions of Les laboureurs’ production\, and considers parall
 els between technology-driven global change in the late nineteenth century
  and in our current day. The exhibition includes microscope images reveali
 ng the\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-10 09:54 PDT
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
END:VEVENT
